#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184074 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184175 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d702975-166e-5067-ae3c-1152fade8248" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance Between a Vector and a Subspace"}] :question/id #uuid "edd4d491-c483-5004-b30f-68cf0ef76f43" :question/math-academy-id "e-5922" :question/problem "Find the distance between the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors $\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 \\},$ where\n![](images/51/5154eac29b8dee2a4f1ae4212306f80d5ff7975d38751a222ef2027d35acc234.svg)" :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $\\mathbf{x}$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{proj}_{S} \\: \\mathbf{x} = A(A^T\\!A)^{-1}\\!A^T\\,\\mathbf{x}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n![](images/ac/acee6cac9fd5dec811783141ecdcfd07402d6482146cdbdcac8f6e536416f0b7.svg)\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}4 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 18\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}9 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance between $\\mathbf{x}$ and the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d(x,\\overset{^}{x}) & =‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{4}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3-(-3))^{2}+(5-5)^{2}+(-1-1)^{2}+(3-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+0+4+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184075 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184176 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26b41192-9680-55c3-930c-52ff235e1800" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto the Solution Space of a Linear System"}] :question/id #uuid "04cb9ecc-68fa-546e-aa96-8a1ee050bbed" :question/math-academy-id "e-5923" :question/problem "Given the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $\\mathbf{x}$ onto the solution space of the system.\n![](images/5a/5ad675762a16e4c81d5d83161dc24646121e4ca10b1e8a4957d7e9a317fc1fc4.svg)" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a basis for the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, $x_2,$ and $x_3$ are free variables. Now, from the first equation, we get $x_1 = 2x_2-3x_3.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n![](images/fe/fe0dd0d87977a4b16d56a96e54a5db6b56bd7cb9f5182a9c43ff6e14f03d2c7a.svg)\n\nConsequently, \n\n![](images/93/9335bf579d464c3e54a92459199d585c8e42b5ef21ee9382436439d050338c9e.svg)\nis a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nNow, we let $A$ be a matrix whose columns equal the elements of $\\mathcal B,$ and we find the orthogonal projection of $\\mathbf{x}$ onto the solution space of the system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}5 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 10\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}10 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184111 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184207 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1224e2dd-96bc-5c24-aacf-3c36a7c3a1e1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Acute Angle Between a Vector and a Subspace"}] :question/id #uuid "98aed663-0f72-5494-9a5f-ba2fdf94764a" :question/math-academy-id "e-9906" :question/problem "Find the acute angle between the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors $\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2\\},$ where\n![](images/13/13b2b59a69e2fd1562f9b835128a16332c7fbd32646f662efe7dbf06bf5cac56.svg)" :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $\\mathbf{x}$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{proj}_{S} \\: \\mathbf{x} = A(A^T\\!A)^{-1}\\!A^T\\,\\mathbf{x}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n![](images/bb/bb65806cb07e71dc92a5c55c210df1112da1f2500ed6cf18ef2a373d155aea94.svg)\nTherefore, we get the following projection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}27 & 9 \\\\ 9 & 27\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{72}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe acute angle between $\\mathbf{x}$ and $S$ is the acute angle between $\\mathbf{x}$ and $\\textrm{proj}_S \\mathbf{x}.$ Equivalently, it is the acute angle between $\\mathbf{x}$ and any non-zero vector that is parallel to $\\textrm{proj}_S \\mathbf{x}.$ So, to make calculations easier, we can find the angle between the vectors\n\n![](images/54/54a3c6bd24d0c021c0aa65ca1f12c6470b83744c46f984bdb076287b076fc9c1.svg)\n\nComputing the cosine using the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{0\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\sqrt{{(-1)}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arccos\\left( \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}2\\right)= \\dfrac\\pi 4,\n$$\n\nwhich is already an acute angle, as desired."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369707 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184175 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d702975-166e-5067-ae3c-1152fade8248" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance Between a Vector and a Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4510b5a-0eac-5993-9918-d9ef0c8a3c71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369709} {:answer/id #uuid "5176f4b5-9d88-5e36-ba8f-d117fff9056d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369710} {:answer/id #uuid "fbf8727a-1e2c-5dbd-8acd-b00ffb3890a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369711} {:answer/id #uuid "52db803f-b52e-537c-b259-1cea943de0de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369712} {:answer/id #uuid "d377623d-2f0c-5b3a-b716-dd9c3e18c9dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52db803f-b52e-537c-b259-1cea943de0de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369712} :answer-field/id #uuid "cad1e1c5-76ad-5b4a-b71b-bd50e6962b71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369708}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "19d894d5-7687-5e09-9d5f-1b801edf3c6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-139472" :question/problem "Find the distance between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}18 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{18}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d(x,\\overset{^}{x}) & =‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2-(-1))^{2}+(2-(-1))^{2}+(5-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+9+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{27} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416323 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184175 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d702975-166e-5067-ae3c-1152fade8248" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance Between a Vector and a Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f092c3d-8556-5f6a-af54-6cf54502714d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416311} {:answer/id #uuid "1a899cfc-2b1e-5341-b7ff-75e82ccc677e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416312} {:answer/id #uuid "ee402ce0-013b-55b8-989b-cc8ea6267cb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416317} {:answer/id #uuid "eef9c29f-2ba3-5765-9533-90dd311f676f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416318} {:answer/id #uuid "facc80f1-1b35-55ea-977b-cfdffdd16d9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a899cfc-2b1e-5341-b7ff-75e82ccc677e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416312} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba894365-a618-5f73-93d7-cf99f582f802" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c0bd3b27-d4c9-5213-b407-098030561a8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-139473" :question/problem "Find the distance between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}8 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 6\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{16}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d(x,\\overset{^}{x}) & =‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3-3)^{2}+(6-1)^{2}+(4-(-1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{50} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416358 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184175 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d702975-166e-5067-ae3c-1152fade8248" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance Between a Vector and a Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29430249-c511-5b3f-b606-e04e258a7382" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416328} {:answer/id #uuid "66516586-cecd-5e63-b1f0-d497a546cd06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416334} {:answer/id #uuid "b038fe34-a16a-5a55-bf98-fc3b8439343d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416342} {:answer/id #uuid "d9c0d55a-c5e9-50c2-8df7-9355a909c1d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416346} {:answer/id #uuid "f15ad28f-93e2-5d8b-b5d3-7600366bd867" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29430249-c511-5b3f-b606-e04e258a7382" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416328} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b507b6b-07ae-51ff-8ef0-2463cc379cda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416353}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d93f91c3-07ee-5843-9236-38543eb4a92a" :question/math-academy-id "q-139474" :question/problem "Find the distance between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{11}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d(x,\\overset{^}{x}) & =‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2-0)^{2}+(6-0)^{2}+(2-0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+36+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{44} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269227 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184207 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1224e2dd-96bc-5c24-aacf-3c36a7c3a1e1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Acute Angle Between a Vector and a Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "206f844b-a9aa-543a-b13a-3a4acc9da6a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266430} {:answer/id #uuid "9605b247-8a44-51d4-bd86-9cbc5c513452" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267482} {:answer/id #uuid "9d07c8ea-8eb0-51e5-9466-d659439c9524" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267555} {:answer/id #uuid "9e8a4161-e6e2-529a-abea-93d855445919" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267572} {:answer/id #uuid "fe6d2f84-0611-5fed-a6aa-de2e286504b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268384}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e8a4161-e6e2-529a-abea-93d855445919" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267572} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e74f88c-8d6d-562e-9858-e61dad89652f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268686}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0761cfb5-82f2-5ff1-afcd-0792aa3de132" :question/math-academy-id "q-139475" :question/problem "Find the acute angle between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}5 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 14\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}14 & -8 \\\\ -8 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe acute angle between $x$ and $S$ is the acute angle between $x$ and ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ Equivalently, it is the acute angle between $x$ and any non-zero vector that is parallel to ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ So, to make calculations easier, we can find the angle between the vectors\n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,2\\,{\\text{proj}}_{S}x=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nComputing the cosine using the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{(-1)\\cdot (-3)+(-1)\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 3}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{6}\\sqrt{18}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})=\\frac{\\pi }{6},\n$$\n\nwhich is already an acute angle."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269228 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184207 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1224e2dd-96bc-5c24-aacf-3c36a7c3a1e1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Acute Angle Between a Vector and a Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06ab9f5c-f9b0-5dd6-918a-bb731247e079" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266201} {:answer/id #uuid "0a2f65bb-4526-584f-856f-27215c1529ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266236} {:answer/id #uuid "21b515ce-8113-511c-85a0-cd526375bb7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266446} {:answer/id #uuid "39bf3cee-b002-50a4-ac7c-283a66da8f06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266653} {:answer/id #uuid "90a4c538-7615-5efa-b16c-ec8c0f84764b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267432}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90a4c538-7615-5efa-b16c-ec8c0f84764b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267432} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1bfa4e5-ee67-5872-a778-8cac048ea831" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268784}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1a3f9a9b-9c5c-5941-8f74-a42675358e73" :question/math-academy-id "q-139477" :question/problem "Find the acute angle between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}9 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe acute angle between $x$ and $S$ is the acute angle between $x$ and ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ Equivalently, it is the acute angle between $x$ and any non-zero vector that is parallel to ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ So, to make calculations easier, we can find the angle between the vectors\n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,2\\,{\\text{proj}}_{S}x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nComputing the cosine using the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{0\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1}\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=\\frac{\\pi }{4},\n$$\n\nwhich is already an acute angle."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269229 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184207 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1224e2dd-96bc-5c24-aacf-3c36a7c3a1e1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Acute Angle Between a Vector and a Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b1719c2-cbaf-5a8a-8ad8-6d7f32d5f2cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266244} {:answer/id #uuid "99fb8f73-5ddb-5794-8d92-72d920d52b65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267537} {:answer/id #uuid "d47ccd6e-8624-5b7c-9993-a19ea7edac40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268040} {:answer/id #uuid "e7478d11-b7f3-5a15-be65-b95013b60046" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268194} {:answer/id #uuid "f487078a-66cc-52f3-bdfd-0b205ae902e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7478d11-b7f3-5a15-be65-b95013b60046" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268194} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd83e725-b731-57f9-a6b5-a6f89fe153b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268776}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "12bd1922-22fd-5b46-aa73-11894915ba39" :question/math-academy-id "q-139478" :question/problem "Find the acute angle between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 27\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{18}[\\begin{aligned}27 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe acute angle between $x$ and $S$ is the acute angle between $x$ and ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ Equivalently, it is the acute angle between $x$ and any non-zero vector that is parallel to ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ So, to make calculations easier, we can find the angle between the vectors\n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,2\\,{\\text{proj}}_{S}x=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].$\n\nComputing the cosine using the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{(-6)\\cdot (-3)+(-3)\\cdot 3+3\\cdot 6}{\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{3}^{2}}\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{3}^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{\\sqrt{54}\\sqrt{54}} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{54} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{\\pi }{3},\n$$\n\nwhich is already an acute angle."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269233 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184207 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1224e2dd-96bc-5c24-aacf-3c36a7c3a1e1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Acute Angle Between a Vector and a Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b09663d-300e-5ee5-8466-82d21294665d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{22.73}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266523} {:answer/id #uuid "4e24ae49-2513-5475-9c72-110a755c76e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{24.11}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266838} {:answer/id #uuid "74ed45fa-c197-5e50-b36d-5a3685a5918c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{27.53}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267170} {:answer/id #uuid "ad689cad-1bb7-5646-b2b3-5e7e409b82ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{19.24}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267710} {:answer/id #uuid "f758adb1-2b16-59b2-ae75-525dfd04d76f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{24.09}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268337}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f758adb1-2b16-59b2-ae75-525dfd04d76f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{24.09}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268337} :answer-field/id #uuid "743f8294-a0bd-590c-8886-d9cce43ee982" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268624}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "27ff07db-fdfd-5460-9a6e-b2c28eedff32" :question/math-academy-id "q-139513" :question/problem "Find the acute angle between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRound the answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we get the following projection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}11 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 8\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{24}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -8 \\\\ -8 & 11\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe acute angle between $x$ and $S$ is the acute angle between $x$ and ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ Equivalently, it is the acute angle between $x$ and any non-zero vector that is parallel to ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ So, to make calculations easier, we can find the angle between the vectors\n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,2\\,{\\text{proj}}_{S}x=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nComputing the cosine using the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{x\\cdot {\\text{proj}}_{S}x}{‖x‖‖{\\text{proj}}_{S}x‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 5+2\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{5}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{9}\\sqrt{30}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{3\\sqrt{30}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{30}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{30}})≈{24.09}^{∘},\n$$\n\nwhich is already an acute angle."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269235 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184176 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26b41192-9680-55c3-930c-52ff235e1800" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto the Solution Space of a Linear System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "077ffa7c-3579-50f8-a629-29543cf3edba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266208} {:answer/id #uuid "08228ea6-8d2c-50eb-8004-c248a3f115b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266217} {:answer/id #uuid "7094dbae-28a0-55ae-9def-87b8be5cd0ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ 2 \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267136} {:answer/id #uuid "9c66ddaf-074c-5264-9c28-7ad7d51542be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267548} {:answer/id #uuid "9cf3ef5a-4f60-598a-900f-23248a9d25ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267554}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08228ea6-8d2c-50eb-8004-c248a3f115b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266217} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c2d5a0c-af40-5c74-a20d-381405158fa8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268482}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "733dc56e-7cef-5043-973a-1d2c8fd2f794" :question/math-academy-id "q-139516" :question/problem "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 6{x}_{1}-8{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a basis for the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 0 & -8 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}$ are free variables. Now, from the first equation, we get $3{x}_{1}=4{x}_{3}.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{3}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{{x}_{3}}{3}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\}$ is the basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nNow, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 25\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 25\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{25}[\\begin{aligned}25 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 25\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184775 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184176 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26b41192-9680-55c3-930c-52ff235e1800" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto the Solution Space of a Linear System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bd04cf3-0f82-5880-915b-421baec1c8d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392328} {:answer/id #uuid "94ec87bc-b4dc-5e19-982e-5e16668b0ee9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392329} {:answer/id #uuid "037e8461-8d16-565d-8e50-1138bb404110" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392330} {:answer/id #uuid "92804d85-7803-58d2-a103-6f4edc35f482" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392331} {:answer/id #uuid "205d1fda-454a-5e6f-a815-1ed3e0770ad7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392332}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92804d85-7803-58d2-a103-6f4edc35f482" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392331} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc4a8c9e-ca92-5f00-a377-01527563ace3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392327}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "27e616d4-1e96-59b7-b91d-2a687a44a3ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-39858" :question/problem "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}],\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-9{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a basis for the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -9 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}$ are free variables. Now, from the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}$ is the basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nNow, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}10 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 5\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 10\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392361 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184176 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26b41192-9680-55c3-930c-52ff235e1800" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto the Solution Space of a Linear System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c77eba07-dc07-589f-8884-be6f0d03ee21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392363} {:answer/id #uuid "fbcee9a5-69aa-5708-aafe-a127637a0cc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392364} {:answer/id #uuid "893aaa25-971c-54ca-85d4-517d467f5514" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392365} {:answer/id #uuid "becd0ca3-6897-543a-8f9d-60e3e356bb81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392366} {:answer/id #uuid "38a78463-dbb9-5ab1-b897-3e1cd62bb83b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392367}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "893aaa25-971c-54ca-85d4-517d467f5514" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392365} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ca78264-e6c8-572f-88da-a3f19c5a8e15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392362}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "52165617-f2b7-52fc-a5ce-09980394cfc1" :question/math-academy-id "q-40631" :question/problem "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 13 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+8{x}_{2}-6{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 8 & -6 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ are free variables. Now, from the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=4{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}$ is the basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nNow, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 13 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}17 & -12 \\\\ -12 & 10\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{26}[\\begin{aligned}10 & 12 \\\\ 12 & 17\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184852 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184175 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d702975-166e-5067-ae3c-1152fade8248" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance Between a Vector and a Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "240432f6-f2e2-5a9a-b570-365bafb77a66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348759} {:answer/id #uuid "3a4e145f-775b-5cc9-9ed9-4083f2509016" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348972} {:answer/id #uuid "890d62fe-d253-5d4b-8ac2-a19c2b8f75fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349691} {:answer/id #uuid "973f4efe-5a38-51f0-92cc-f6a38504b41d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349804} {:answer/id #uuid "c516d012-84ee-530e-ac16-264019180d3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350186}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c516d012-84ee-530e-ac16-264019180d3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350186} :answer-field/id #uuid "403aa802-b10a-5e94-9e23-00130286699e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350817}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "16d7e659-66cb-54f0-b03c-983af77b46e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-83617" :question/problem "Find the distance between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d(x,\\overset{^}{x}) & =‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3-2)^{2}+(-3-(-1))^{2}+(0-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354515 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184175 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d702975-166e-5067-ae3c-1152fade8248" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance Between a Vector and a Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08980956-49e2-55ae-a196-45fb6c214439" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351644} {:answer/id #uuid "14c3270c-306f-59b8-b413-7e985a55dd61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351750} {:answer/id #uuid "17cc70ea-934a-54d2-801b-50ae5ecbaa9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351782} {:answer/id #uuid "7c57c8e1-d85d-5348-b332-ffe02792e22f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352656} {:answer/id #uuid "b49c04b6-e090-5072-af05-31e8d754e4a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353112}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b49c04b6-e090-5072-af05-31e8d754e4a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353112} :answer-field/id #uuid "585e15a6-aa1c-57ac-afb3-e53c85938b75" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353973}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1a981f64-b6ae-500a-bc22-bdc38fa48eab" :question/math-academy-id "q-86822" :question/problem "Find the distance between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d(x,\\overset{^}{x}) & =‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{4}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(0-1)^{2}+(0-(-1))^{2}+(3-2)^{2}+(1-0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1+1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354518 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184207 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1224e2dd-96bc-5c24-aacf-3c36a7c3a1e1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Acute Angle Between a Vector and a Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0321347d-f889-5169-a954-ad53ad6e3f2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{32.54}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351592} {:answer/id #uuid "69ebb229-ddaa-5394-b197-c67dc5a728a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{37}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352506} {:answer/id #uuid "865713b7-36a4-53bf-bb66-1513a3d90bee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{21}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352735} {:answer/id #uuid "c9d0d3b7-943b-501d-9dda-94bed23beb55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{19.47}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353323} {:answer/id #uuid "dad94daf-b403-53d4-9765-1b9e1321c6bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45.77}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9d0d3b7-943b-501d-9dda-94bed23beb55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{19.47}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353323} :answer-field/id #uuid "3828b66d-f82a-5813-9ed6-8d2fc865ed33" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353910}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "520b11ad-97ee-56c3-9607-d0a21f040e1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-86829" :question/problem "Find the acute angle between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRound the answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe acute angle between $x$ and $S$ is the acute angle between $x$ and ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ Equivalently, it is the acute angle between $x$ and any non-zero vector that is parallel to ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ So, to make calculations easier, we can find the angle between the vectors\n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,3\\,{\\text{proj}}_{S}x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nComputing the cosine using the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot (-4)}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{3}\\sqrt{24}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{3}\\sqrt{3\\cdot 8}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{3})≈{19.47}^{∘},\n$$\n\nwhich is already an acute angle."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354522 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184176 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26b41192-9680-55c3-930c-52ff235e1800" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto the Solution Space of a Linear System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47950cdc-9011-5627-871f-a8b1447968f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352228} {:answer/id #uuid "8d9949bc-72e9-589f-8ec6-ce3aa779db9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352803} {:answer/id #uuid "ce89b567-943b-5e39-8ea7-24816b3999a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353358} {:answer/id #uuid "cfa7447d-9ea1-57b1-8706-b646e61e044c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353363} {:answer/id #uuid "dc216c09-bb8d-5b18-aa7c-78f1dedc3d4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47950cdc-9011-5627-871f-a8b1447968f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352228} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebb662fb-1008-5c8c-bc2f-fdcbbf66b9f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354218}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ef3c7964-4e2c-5455-96eb-f43a3074ac27" :question/math-academy-id "q-86844" :question/problem "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a basis for the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}$ are free variables. Now, from the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=2{x}_{3}.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}$ is the basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nNow, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416357 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184176 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26b41192-9680-55c3-930c-52ff235e1800" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto the Solution Space of a Linear System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "453ed560-2a6a-584b-b775-2ac6a73e45b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416330} {:answer/id #uuid "4e677ef6-4718-55df-b04f-5323f885a475" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416332} {:answer/id #uuid "75d24566-becf-5714-8a17-ca7340070ab8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416335} {:answer/id #uuid "a4e29b1a-ee23-527d-a4ce-26194d144439" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416340} {:answer/id #uuid "b7f21d52-3d12-5f8b-8383-908db610799b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7f21d52-3d12-5f8b-8383-908db610799b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416343} :answer-field/id #uuid "9de09353-fb9c-544f-8c67-c4ef2c4abd36" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416354}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "15ea3713-dc0a-53ca-b70c-c22a6b79a105" :question/math-academy-id "q-86853" :question/problem "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a basis for the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}$ are free variables. Now, from the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}.$ Therefore, the general solution is \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}$ is the basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nNow, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
